&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience, ideally including exposure to data-heavy products in experimentation, analytics, or fintech domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own an end-to-end product lifecycle in fast-paced, high-stakes environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense - the ability to identify customer problems worth solving and prioritize ruthlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with experimentation and analytics (A/B testing, statistical significance, metrics, funnels) to inform product decisions, and partnering with engineering/data teams on pipeline and dashboard topics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of strong cross-functional influence and excellent written communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data visualization best practices and user-centered design for technical audiences; you draw influence from Tufte&#39;s ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in building developer tools or productivity platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with SQL and comfort working in notebooks or prototyping with basic datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a high-autonomy team environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with economics or ROI measurement frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise SaaS tools and security/privacy considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior exposure to GenAI products and/or AI-enhanced user interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
